# Rank 1098 / CVE-2026-33979: express-xss-sanitizer treats an explicit empty
# `allowedTags: []` or `allowedAttributes: {}` as unset and falls back to
# sanitize-html's permissive defaults (CWE-79, CWE-183).
#
# CAUGHT by omission: `sanitize()` is not a known HtmlEscape control, so an
# HTML-render sink downstream expects VYQL-INJ-004 on the empty-allowlist call.
# The same unrecognized call would still report on the fixed library version.
#
# verify_current_expected: caught-by-omission

test "rank1098: sanitize is called with an explicit empty allowlist"
  lang javascript
  file app.js
  expect VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  const { sanitize } = require('express-xss-sanitizer');

  function handler(req, res) {
    const bio = req.query.bio;
    const clean = sanitize(bio, { allowedTags: [], allowedAttributes: {} });
    res.send('<div>' + clean + '</div>');
  }
  ```
